{"tool_name":"clair3-trio","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"clair3-trio","home":"https://github.com/HKU-BAL/Clair3-Trio","license":"BSD-3-Clause","summary":"High-performance Nanopore long-read variant calling in family trios with Trio-to-Trio deep neural networks.","addition_date":"2023-01-22T01:12:25.794991Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:11:11.429000Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:clair3-trio","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"name":"Syed Shakeel Ahmed"},{"name":"Junhao Su","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-8560-3999"},{"name":"Ruibang Luo","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-9711-6533"},{"name":"Tak-Wah Lam","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4676-8587"},{"name":"Zhenxian Zheng","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-6546-2324"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Network analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3927"},{"term":"Variant calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227"}]}],"maturity":"Legacy","name":"Clair3-Trio","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bib/bbac301","metadata":{"abstract":"Accurate identification of genetic variants from family child-mother-father trio sequencing data is important in genomics. However, state-of-the-art approaches treat variant calling from trios as three independent tasks, which limits their calling accuracy for Nanopore long-read sequencing data. For better trio variant calling, we introduce Clair3-Trio, the first variant caller tailored for family trio data from Nanopore long-reads. Clair3-Trio employs a Trio-to-Trio deep neural network model, which allows it to input the trio sequencing information and output all of the trio's predicted variants within a single model to improve variant calling. We also present MCVLoss, a novel loss function tailor-made for variant calling in trios, leveraging the explicit encoding of the Mendelian inheritance. Clair3-Trio showed comprehensive improvement in experiments. It predicted far fewer Mendelian inheritance violation variations than current state-of-the-art methods. We also demonstrated that our Trio-to-Trio model is more accurate than competing architectures. Clair3-Trio is accessible as a free, open-source project at https://github.com/HKU-BAL/Clair3-Trio.","authors":[{"name":"Ahmed S.S."},{"name":"Lam T.-W."},{"name":"Luo R."},{"name":"Su J."},{"name":"Zheng Z."}],"citationCount":5,"date":"2022-09-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Briefings in Bioinformatics","title":"Clair3-trio: High-performance Nanopore long-read variant calling in family trios with trio-to-trio deep neural networks"},"pmcid":"PMC9487642","pmid":"35849103"}],"topic":[{"term":"Genetics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3053"},{"term":"Laboratory techniques","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3361"},{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Clair3-Trio","home":"https://bio.tools/clair3-trio","license":"BSD-3-Clause","summary":"High-performance Nanopore long-read variant calling in family trios with Trio-to-Trio deep neural networks.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:clair3-trio/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":27,"citations":[{"count":3,"year":"2024"},{"count":4,"year":"2023"},{"count":5,"year":"2026"},{"count":15,"year":"2025"}],"doi":"10.1093/bib/bbac301","pmcid":"PMC9487642","pmid":"35849103","ref_count":18,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"2010"},{"count":1,"year":"2015"},{"count":1,"year":"2016"},{"count":1,"year":"2018"},{"count"